<figure class="vac-figure" aria-labelledby="vac-ret-title" data-vac-retention>
  <figcaption id="vac-ret-title"><span>Figure 1</span> A committed price can still need its old tuple</figcaption>
  <div class="vac-scene">
    <div class="vac-readers" data-live>
      <div><b>Report R · earlier snapshot</b><strong data-report>20.00</strong><small data-report-state>Snapshot established</small></div>
      <div><b>New reader · after commit</b><strong data-new>Not started</strong><small>Independent ordinary read</small></div>
    </div>
    <p class="vac-stage" data-stage data-live>Report R has run its first SELECT.</p>
    <div class="vac-heap" data-live>
      <p class="vac-label">Products · illustrative heap page</p>
      <div class="vac-tuple" data-old><b>P7 · 20.00</b><span data-old-state>Current tuple</span></div>
      <div class="vac-tuple vac-new" data-fresh><b data-fresh-value>Free space</b><span data-fresh-state>Room for a later version</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="vac-index" data-live><b>Price index → heap tuples</b><span data-index>20.00 → earlier tuple</span></div>
    <div class="vac-maps" data-live><p>Free space map <b data-fsm>No reclaimed space yet</b></p><p>All-visible bit <b data-vm>Clear in this model</b></p></div>
    <p class="vac-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The read-only Repeatable Read report establishes its snapshot while P7 costs 20.00.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="vac-options"><label for="vac-other">Other retention</label><select id="vac-other"><option value="none">Only report R</option><option value="other">Another earlier snapshot remains</option></select></div>
  <div class="vac-controls" role="group" aria-label="Playback for figure 1"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 6</span></div><div class="vac-hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
  <p class="vac-caption">A model of P7’s independent 20.00 → 22.00 replay. A local B-tree on <code>price</code> makes this a non-HOT update, so both versions have index entries. Placement and cleanup steps are illustrative; unrelated products and index pages are omitted.</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><ol><li>Report R establishes a snapshot showing 20.00.</li><li>The writer updates P7 and commits. A new reader sees 22.00; R still sees 20.00.</li><li>Vacuum runs, but cannot remove the earlier tuple while that snapshot needs it.</li><li>R ends. Another earlier snapshot, if selected, still retains the tuple.</li><li>A later vacuum can remove the old tuple and obsolete index entry only after all relevant retention has ended.</li><li>The reclaimed space is available inside the same heap file. The all-visible bit can be set once the page qualifies.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-vac-retention]')) {
 const q=(s:string)=>root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(s)!;
 const choice=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('select')!;
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>6,draw:(step:number)=>{
  const other=choice.value==='other',updated=step>=1,ended=step>=3,clean=step>=4&&!other;
  q('[data-report]').textContent=ended?'Finished':'20.00';
  q('[data-report-state]').textContent=ended?'Snapshot released':'Earlier snapshot retained';
  q('[data-new]').textContent=updated?'22.00':'Not started';
  q('[data-old]') .classList.toggle('vac-free',clean);
  q('[data-old] b').textContent=clean?'Reusable space':'P7 · 20.00';
  q('[data-old-state]').textContent=clean?'Old tuple removed':updated?'Replaced, still retained':'Current tuple';
  q('[data-fresh-value]').textContent=updated?'P7 · 22.00':'Free space';
  q('[data-fresh-state]').textContent=updated?'Committed new tuple':'Room for a later version';
  q('[data-index]').textContent=clean?'22.00 → new tuple':updated?'20.00 → earlier tuple · 22.00 → new tuple':'20.00 → earlier tuple';
  q('[data-fsm]').textContent=clean?'Reclaimed bytes available':'No reclaimed space yet';
  q('[data-vm]').textContent=step===5&&!other?'Set · page qualifies':'Clear in this model';
  const stages=['Report R has run its first SELECT.','The writer commits the new price.','Vacuum runs while R keeps its snapshot.','Report R ends its transaction.',clean?'A later vacuum removes obsolete material.':'A later vacuum still meets retained history.',other?'The second snapshot still holds cleanup back.':'Reusable space; the heap file has not shrunk.'];
  const explanations=[
   'The read-only Repeatable Read report establishes its snapshot while P7 costs 20.00.',
   'Commit makes 22.00 available to a new snapshot. It does not make the earlier 20.00 tuple removable: report R still needs it.',
   'Vacuum finishes without reclaiming this old tuple. Repeating the same work cannot override the report’s retained view.',
   other?'R releases its snapshot, but another earlier snapshot remains. Finishing one report has not removed the last retention requirement.':'R releases the last relevant snapshot in this branch. The tuple is now eligible for cleanup; its bytes have not yet been reclaimed.',
   other?'The second snapshot still needs 20.00. Vacuum must retain its tuple and index entry.':'A later vacuum removes the obsolete index entry and old tuple. The free space map can advertise the reclaimed heap space for reuse.',
   other?'The second snapshot must end before this old tuple can be reclaimed. No setting can make vacuum safely erase a version that a retained view needs.':'The page can now be marked all-visible. A suitable index-only scan can avoid fetching it, while later writes can reuse its free bytes. The file still contains this page.'
  ];
  q('[data-stage]').textContent=stages[step];q('[data-explanation]').textContent=explanations[step];
 }});
 choice.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
}
</script>
